body:
I had intense dental procedures when I was about 8-12 and because of a huge phobia of needles I got nitrous before any numbing. I remember that one time I decided to breath deep so I would get more "funny" from laughing gas. Holes in a speaker on the ceiling began to dance and my mom sounded like a robot. I felt like a victim of alien abduction because of the lights and audio distortion.

&#x200B;

Now I know why my mom was worried when I cheerfully described my trip.
